{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we need to find the volume of the tetrahedron generated by the vectors \\(\\mathbf{a}\\), \\(\\mathbf{b}\\), and \\(\\mathbf{c}\\) and use the given volume to find the value of \\(3 \\cos^2 \\theta - 2 \\cos^3 \\theta\\).\n\n### Step 1: Volume of the Tetrahedron\nThe volume \\(V\\) of the tetrahedron formed by vectors \\(\\mathbf{a}\\), \\(\\mathbf{b}\\), and \\(\\mathbf{c}\\) can be expressed using the scalar triple product:\n\\[\nV = \\frac{1}{6} \\left| \\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}) \\right|\n\\]\nGiven that the volume is \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{360}}\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{6} \\left| \\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}) \\right| = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{360}}\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Magnitude of the Cross Product\nSince \\(\\mathbf{a}\\), \\(\\mathbf{b}\\), and \\(\\mathbf{c}\\) are unit vectors, the magnitude of the cross product \\(\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\left| \\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c} \\right| = \\sin \\theta\n\\]\nThus, the volume can be rewritten as:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{6} \\left| \\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}) \\right| = \\frac{1}{6} \\left| \\mathbf{a} \\right| \\left| \\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c} \\right| \\sin \\theta = \\frac{1}{6} \\sin \\theta\n\\]\n\n","prefix_end":1169,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1184,311,1477,279,8123,315,279,27853,32507,291,2248,7907,553,279,22879,1124,11520,10374,13233,90,64,11035,701,1124,11520,10374,13233,90,65,11035,701,323,1124,11520,10374,13233,90,66,11035,8,323,990,279,2661,8123,311,1477,279,897,315,17767,18,1124,9407,61,17,1124,15976,481,220,17,1124,9407,61,18,1124,15976,59,3593,14374,14822,220,16,25,20265,315,279,49762,32507,291,2248,198,785,8123,17767,53,57758,315,279,27853,32507,291,2248,14122,553,22879,1124,11520,10374,13233,90,6